Package: knowledge
Title: Tests Fish Habitat Definitions Against What is Known About Where Fish
    Live, and Tunes Them from the Fish Records
Version: 0.4.36
Date: 2026-11-12
Authors@R: c(
    person("Allan", "Irvine", , "al@newgraphenvironment.com", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-3495-2128",
                       affiliation = "New Graph Environment Ltd.")),
    person("New Graph Environment Ltd.", role = c("cph", "fnd"))
    )
Description: Gathers what is known about where fish live in British
    Columbia's streams (each species' life history from the cited literature
    with its quotes, past reports, intrinsic-potential models, life-history
    timing and the provincial fish sampling records) and tunes from the
    records the gradient and stream-size thresholds of the fish habitat
    definitions the link habitat models use: it places sampling visits on
    link's stream segments, scores candidate habitat definitions on held-out
    watershed groups, grades segments by expected use, and tabulates, maps
    and compares the tuned habitat definitions with link's defaults. It also pulls PSCIS crossing layers
    and past-report tables for a group and checks stream names before a
    search. Under active development.
